<<~ ahu slot=`#/contract`>>

!! Contract

`base-doc.ts` owns the shapes every plane shares and the one primitive that
turns a bag-URI into a live doc handle:

* ''`LarDoc` / `LarTiddlerRecord` / `LarBlobEntry`'' — the Automerge document
  shape (`tiddlers` map + `blobs` map) and its record/blob entries.
* ''`mutableLarRecord(title, fields, provenance)`'' — the record builder every
  writer routes through, stamping `meta.authority`.
* ''`ENGINE_CORE_ID`'' (`"tiddlywikicore"`) — the primary `.blobs` key for the
  TW5 boot kernel.
* ''`blobDescriptorUri(blobId)`'' → `lar:///ha.ka.ba/bags/oracle/blobs/<safe>`.
  Blobs live in the ''`@oracle`'' runtime system island beside the engine
  bytes — never in the `lararium` corpus seed (the 2026-06-16 carve; see
  `disk-projection#oracle-split`).
* ''`resolveCatalogRow(registryHandle, rowKey, resolve, provenance)`'' — the
  read → resolve → write-back-on-first-mint shape for a bag→doc pointer.
  Reads the pointer (`text` field) from the registry doc; hands the URL (or
  null) to the platform `resolve` strategy; writes the row back
  only on first mint. Platform divergence rides the two arguments (`resolve`
  = repo strategy, `provenance` = authority stamp), never the protocol.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/two-plane`>>

!! One owner per registry (W26 slice 2, 2026-10-18)

`resolveCatalogRow` takes the ''registry handle'' as an argument and stays plane-blind: it writes wherever the handed
handle points. Today every caller (`open-vessel-core`) hands the vessel's own `@catalog`, so each vessel's bag→doc rows
rest in its own registry and no shared `@oracle` registry carries a pointer. The system bags `lares` and `lararium` carry
no catalog row at all: their live documents rest in the Kahu realm (`kahu-realm.ts`, `realm-bag.ts`), and the genesis
island document is the floor's read-face (`wiki-layer-ontology#oracle-planes`).

<<~/ahu>>

